{"Title":"An Act to restore the effective date of MassHealth coverage for new applicants","BillNumber":"S729","DocketNumber":"SD1187","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BPC0","Name":"Brendan P. Crighton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BPC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T10:31:35.523"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BPC0","Name":"Brendan P. Crighton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BPC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T10:31:35.5233333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S729/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Crighton, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 729) of Brendan P. Crighton for legislation to restore the effective date of MassHealth coverage for new applicants.  Health Care Financing.","DocumentText":"\tSection 9A of chapter 118E of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting the following new section:-\r\n\t(17) For applicants under age 65 who submit all required eligibility verifications within the time determined by the division, the start date of coverage shall begin on the first day of the third calendar month before the month of application.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[{"FiscalType":null,"Amount":"More Than 100,000.00 "}],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J24","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J24"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}